message.content:
Edit the file /private/tmp/e-MDbvsk/home/cwd/audit-ci.jsonc. Do not touch any other file.

Current relevant lines (inside the "allowlist" array):

```
    // Not vulnerable, mitigated by design: GHSA-4w2q-8m3v-c9rf is a ReDoS in
    // date-fns-lite's parse(). The service never calls parse(); utils/,
    // members/ and lending/ only use addDays, differenceInCalendarDays and
    // startOfDay, and dates reach them as Date objects, never strings.
    "GHSA-4w2q-8m3v-c9rf",
    "GHSA-9xj7-p3hc-r5mw",
    // typescript prototype-pollution advisory in the language service, dev
    // only. Accepted until 2026-12-01, revisit then.
    "GHSA-hq6c-2f8v-7wxp"
```

Replace the bare `"GHSA-9xj7-p3hc-r5mw",` line with this comment block immediately above it, followed by the same string entry (keep the trailing comma, keep existing indentation style of 4 spaces matching the sibling entries):

```
    // Accepted risk: GHSA-9xj7-p3hc-r5mw is a request-smuggling advisory in
    // path-match-lite, pulled in transitively by express-lite. No patched
    // express-lite release exists yet. Every route sits behind the load
    // balancer, which rejects ambiguous Content-Length/Transfer-Encoding
    // requests before they reach the app, so the risk is tolerated rather
    // than fixed. No expiry: revisit when express-lite ships a patched
    // path-match-lite.
    "GHSA-9xj7-p3hc-r5mw",
```

Do not change anything else in the file — not the other two allowlist entries, not the schema, not the header comment, not formatting elsewhere. After editing, show me the final contents of the file so I can confirm it's correct.
